      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-12-08_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <head>NO. 817</head>
        <p>NO. 817</p>
        <p>WIRE NETTING, STAPLES, GARDEN TOOLS. CUT, WROUGHT, WIRE AND COPPER NAILS. Bolts and Nuts, Washers, Set Screws, &amp;c. W. Lin J. ELLISON, GENERAL IRONMONGERS, . PARADISE-BT., LIVERPOOL. Telephone, No. 1, 745</p>
        <p>56, BRIDGE-STREET, WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>3IRs. NICHOLSON,</p>
        <p>Having purchased a Large Consignment of NEW &amp; ARTISTIC GOODS,</p>
        <p>Suitable for Presents and for the Christmas Season,</p>
        <p>Invites an inspection from her friends and customers. During the Christmas Season A DISCOUNT OF FIVE PER CENT. WILL BE ALLOWED ON CASH SALES, OF FIVE SHILLINCkS AND UPWARDS.</p>
        <p>GRATIS WITH THE EXAMINER.</p>
        <p>ON SATURDAY NEXT, DEC. 15TE, OUR</p>
        <p>ANNUAL SHEET ALMANAC</p>
        <p>Printed in two colours upon toned paper WILL BE PRESENTED TO EACH PURCHASER OF THE EXAMINER.</p>
        <p>THE SHEET WILL BE ADORNED WITH A</p>
        <p>VIEW OF WINDSOR CASTLE AND WILL CONTAIN MANY NEW FEATURES EMBODYING A LARGE AMOUNT OF</p>
        <p>LOCAL AND GENERAL INFORMATION.</p>
        <p>ARVERTISERS</p>
        <p>WILL DO WELL TO AVAIL THEMSELVES OF THE LARGELY INCREASED CIRCULATION.</p>
        <p>OF THE EXAMINER ON ALMANAC DAY.</p>
        <p>NEWSAGENTS ARE REQUESTED TO ORDER EARLY.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-12-08_WidnesExaminer_art0002" n="art0002">
        <head>REGISTERED FOR TRANSMISSION ABROAD</head>
        <p>REGISTERED FOR TRANSMISSION ABROAD</p>
        <p>SATURDAY, DECEMBER 8, 1894</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-12-08_WidnesExaminer_art0003" n="art0003">
        <p>RUNCORN URBAN DISTRICT COUNCIL ELECTION.</p>
        <p>TO THE ELECTORS OF HEATH WARD.</p>
        <p>LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,-</p>
        <p>The passing of the Local Government Bill brings us fans to face with a new era in municipal government, and the Board of Commissioners now gives place to a District Council. Another matter new to Runcorn is the division of the town into wards. This is a subject that has engaged my earnest attention. I was honoured by .the Cheshire County Council to be one of the committee to conduct the inquiry with refer nee to the su6ject. and their recommendation was approved by the Council. This, in my opinion, will enable the electors to have more complet: control over their repre- sentatives, as they will be able to draw their-a.' tention to any matters requiring the consideration of the District Council. My views on the subject of education generally are well known to you. I consider it absolutely necessary that the young people of tee present day shou'd have the full benefits arising from the grants which the County Council are now giving, and it is eneinently satisfactory ta and that Runcorn Is ha the front rank of all urban districts, as they have been recipirnts of not simply yearly grants for the purposes of higher education, but a handsome sum towards the new Technical Institute, which is approaching completion My sincere hope is that full a,wentage will be taken of the opportunities provided by the new Institute by these wishing to make progress in the world. My dual position as a Commissioner and County Councillor has enabled me tol ok after the true interests of the town in this matter and you may rely upon the best interests of Run- corn receiving in the future, as in the past,my best care and attention.</p>
        <p>You are all aware of the great depression that exists at the present moment in the town, and one of the things that I think will facilitate an improvement is the immediate carry- ing out of the agreement of September, 1890, existing between the Commissioners and the Ship Canal Co. with respect to the provision of a graving do k. I have hitherto zealously laboured to bring this about, and shall continue my efforts to this end, so that vessels arrivinz at Runcorn will not be com- pelled to go eisewh3re for repairs. This will revive an old industry that gave labour to a large number of carpenters and others.</p>
        <p>The acquisition of the Water Works by the Commissioners has proved of deeided benefit to the town, for, although numerous difficulties have been encountered during the first year. a substantial profit has resulted. This bears out my expressed anticipations when the scheme was considered by you. The health of the town is one deserving the closest atten- tion of your representatives, and the increasei activity ors the part of the Health Committee during the past two years has met with my warmest support The reduct on Is the death-rate of late must be gratifying to all of you. All sani- tnry improvements shall always receive my earnest atten- tion. There are many other subjects which will call for the attention of your representatives.which Will include, amongst others, the provision of a recrestion ground. This has my entire sympathy, and shall receive, together with all matters affe ling the bet interests of the town, my most earnest consideration.</p>
        <p>It must have been gratifying to you, as ratepayers, to have found your burdens somewhat lightened by the contribution of a further 2200 a year. making in all, 2400 per annum by the County Council for the maintenance of the main roads of tl e town.</p>
        <p>'confidently appeal to you for a renewal of your confi- dence which has been uninterrupted for over twenty years, and if elected upon the new Urban District Council. you may rely upon my best efforts being devoted to carefully watch all matters concerning the welfare and advancement of our town. - - - ••</p>
        <p>I am, Lades and Gentlemen, Yours faithfully. PHILIP SPEAKMAN.</p>
        <p>The Mount, Higher Runcorn, 29th, November, 1894.</p>
        <p>;</p>
        <p>it they lose on I „ intending</p>
        <p>-A</p>
        <p>R. ISHERWOOD, HOUSE AND COMMISSION AGENT, 57, TANNERS'-LANE, WARRING-TON, Established 1873. Rents and Debts collected.</p>
        <p>Agent for Fire, Life, Accident, Employers' Liability, Live</p>
        <p>Stock and Plate Glass Insurance Co.s.</p>
        <p>ow sit Current Rates, Prompt and Liberal Settlements.</p>
        <p>_ , • -,.</p>
      </div>
