      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-12-08_WidnesExaminer_art0031" n="art0031">
        <head>READ OF FURTHER.</head>
        <p>READ OF FURTHER.</p>
        <p>SPONTANEOUS TEgTIMONY WORTHY OF YOUR CONSIDERATION.</p>
        <p>SIR.—My wife desires me to say that your Tudor Williams Balsam of Honey h:s proved a most valuable medicine in our large family (eignt children). As soon as a cough or a cold makes its appearance a dose of Tudor's Balsam is at once administered, and his treatment is followed up until the cold disappears. Before using the Bilsam in Our family the children have been prostrate with colds for several weeks, but now, by taking doses, as directed they seem to suffer very little inconvenience. During the short time the c-ild is noon them the action or the Balsam is marvellous, and the little ones take it readily and ask for more. WALTER J. BRETT, C.M., March 16th, 1892.</p>
        <p>Headmaster Severn [runnel School.</p>
