      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-12-08_WidnesExaminer_art0033" n="art0033">
        <head>PUBLIC MEN SPEAK HIGHLY OF IT ALL OVER</head>
        <p>PUBLIC MEN SPEAK HIGHLY OF IT ALL OVER</p>
        <p>THE WORLD.</p>
        <p>Dowlais, Merthyr Tydfil, Glamorgan, Julv, 1892. DEAR SIR,—I must write to say that your Tudor Williams Balsam of Honey for Coughs is the best we ever had in the house. My boy David had a cough which shook him front top to toe, couldn'i sleep at night for it, ant neither could anyone else in the house sleep because of his barking. A few doses of Balsam of lloney positively cured him; it is a wonderful cure.</p>
        <p>DAVID JONES, ESQ., High Constable.</p>
