      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-12-08_WidnesExaminer_art0076" n="art0076">
        <head>LYMbI.</head>
        <p>LYMbI.</p>
        <p>POPULAR CONCERT.—A concert was held in the New- field Institute on Saturday night when there was a large attendance. Songs, recitations, iSzc., were given by the fdlowing :—Misses Mersian, Schaub, Gaston, M. Swan- wick, and Messrs. "Metland and Swanwick. A pleasant evening was brought to a close by the singing of" God save the Queen." . FARM FlRE.—A'fire broke out at about six o'clock on Sat urda.s night in the sta.ckyard of Mr. Gould, Foxley Farm. The fire was discovered by a teamsman, and information was at once sent to the Lymm Fire Brigade, who promptly turned out, and found that a stack of second crop of clover was burning furiously. Seeing that it wa; hopeless to try and extinguish the fire, they turned their attention to preventing it spreading to a large amont of corn which was in close proximity to the hurnint crack, and in this they were successful. The fire ia supposed to have been caused by overheating. The ta-hole of the damage is covered by insurance.</p>
      </div>
