      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-12-08_WidnesExaminer_art0092" n="art0092">
        <p>You are interested in money making and no such opportunity for saving money has ever been presented to women who use knitting and fancy wools as that made to the readers of this paper by the Providence Mills Spinning Company. They are willing to send you some beautiful samples of knitting, embroidery, and fancy wools for home knitting whicu may be kept by you. Their object is to show you that for appearance, wear and price they cannot be surpassed. In these days of scarcity of cash it is interesting to know the way to buy the necessaries of life direct from the manufacturers and thereby save threepence or more in each shillings- worth. We confidently recommend yt*u to write to-day for patterns which will be sent free of charge by sending a post-card with your name and address upon it. _Kindly note that letters shpuld be carefully addressed —Providence Mills Spinning Co., C. Department, Brad- ford, Yorkshire. you would like they will alio send you samples of their special dress fabrics as well as particu- lars of their wonderful underwear. EMI</p>
        <p>'</p>
