      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-12-08_WidnesExaminer_art0114" n="art0114">
        <head>ELECTION 0F POOH-LAW GUARDIANS FOR RUNCORN UNION.</head>
        <p>THE ELECTION 0F POOH-LAW GUARDIANS FOR RUNCORN UNION.</p>
        <p>THE NOMINATIONS.</p>
        <p>Contests will take place in all of tho six wards into which Runcorn is divided. The polling takes place on the 15th instant in the same booth as the district coun- cil polls. DALTON WARD.—Samuel Taylor, 3.P., Henry White. MERSEY WARD.—The Rev. John B. Gastaldi, David Henry Jones, Henry White. CENTRAL WARD (two members).—F. S. Carr, S. Coventry, Rev. J. B. Gastaldi, D. H. Jones, T. Lea, Henry White, Rev. Canon Maitland Wood, S. Yarwood. BRIDGEWATER WARD.—D. H. Jones, A. R. Norman, Rev. A. M. Wood. NEWTOWN WARD.—D. H. Jones, T. Lea, Rev. A. M. Wood, S. Yarwood. HEATH WARD: The Rev. J. B. Gastaldi, D. H. Jones, T. Handley, J.P., and A. R. Norman. The following were nominated for guardians and rural district councillors, the asterisk denoting the gentlemen returned unopposed :—Acton Grange (1), *Charles Roylaoce ; Alvanley (1), *A. Greenway ; Antrobus (1), *Rev. lar. N. Tanner; Appleton—Stockton Heath Ward (1) : J. Pemberton, W. Bostock, C. W. Daven- port. Appleton—APpleton Ward (1) : *J. Knowles Aston and Aston Grange (1) : *A. H. Talbot,: J.P. Bartington (1) : *J. ; Lowe. Great Badworth *J. Macintyre. Clifton (1) : *J. Stokes. Crowley (1) : *J. Whitlow. Daresbury and Keckwick (1) : T. Darlington, W. Kearsley, and T. Houghton. Dutton (1) : *T. Baxter. C.C. Frodsharo (2) : J. Edwards, H. E. Heywood, C. E. Linaker, and J. Moseley Williams. Frodsham Lordship (1) : *T. Lewis. Grappenhall (1) : *W. Bradford. Halton (1) *T. Wright. Hattan (1) : *J. Parr. Helsby (1) : J. Brandreth, J. Taylor. Kingsley (1) : J. Norcross and S. Woodward. Kings- wood (1) :W. Ellison. Latchford (Withoo.) no nomina- tion. Manley (1) : *3. rlorton. Moore (1) : J. L.Jones and Bessie Dutton. Newton-bv-Daresbury (1) : Hatton, J. W. Taylor, and E. Bretherton. Norley. (1) : *W Pickering. Norton and Stockham (1) : J. W. Baguley. Preston-o'-the-Hill: *J. Spruce. Seven Oaks and Whit. Icy Superior (1) : *G. Priestner. Stretton (1) : *J- Darbvshire. Sutton (1) : *E. Wallington. Thelwa (1) : *J. R.