        <p>UPPER MERSEY NAVIGATION ACTS 1876 AND 1879. T THE UNDERSIGNED HENRY COLLIER of IL Runcorn in the County of Chester being by writing under the hand of Ai. hur Sinclair Esquire, the Chairman of the Upper Mersey Navigation Comm.ssioners duly appointed the Returning Officer for the Year One thousand eight hun- dred and ninety Sour at the Election of Commissioners under the above mention el Acts do hereby declare that the under- mentioned three persons have been this day duly nominated for the office of Elected Commissioners under the Upper Mersey Navigation Acts 1876 and 1879 and the number of persons so nominated not exceeding the numuer of vacancies I do here y declare the said several persons to be duly Elec- ted Commissioners under the said Acts and such Commis- sioners shall enter on their office on the first day of january now next ensuing. Names ot persons elected as aforesaid. WILLIAM HENRY BODDINGTON ot Sandborough, Altrinsham. Canal Carrier. WILLIAM HENRY COLLIER of Sale,Manche=ter,Manager. Winchester Ship Canal Company Bridgewater Canals, Under taking. CHARLES WHITEWAY HAZLEHURST of Mossley Hill, Liverpool. Soap Manufacturer. Dated at the office of the said Commissioners in Runcorn in the *County of .Chester this first day of December One thousaud.eight hundred and ninety four. HENRY COLLIER Returning Officer.</p>
        <p>CHARITY COMMISSION. In the Matter of the Charity of OLIVER LYME in the Townships of Prescot and Whiston in the Parish of Prescot in the County of Lancaster; and in the Matter of " The Charitable Trusts Act, 1853 to 1894." By direction of the Board of Charity Commissioners far England and Wales, Notice is hereby given that the Trustees of this Charity propose to grant a Building. Lease of the property mentioned in the subjoined Schedule (exclusive of the subjacent minerals) for a term of 999 years from the Ist of November 1894, at an annual rent of £1 9s. 10(1. the Lessee agreeing to expend not less than £2OO in Building. Further particulars may be ascertained from HENRY CROSS of No. 19, Castle-street, Liverpool, solicitor. Any objection or suggestion relative to the proposed Lease may be trAnsmitted to the Commissioners in writing, within 21 idays from the first publication of this Notice, addressed to " The Secretary, Charity Commission, Whitehall, London, , S.W." Dated the 27th day of November, 1894. D. h. FEA RON, Secretary. SCHEDULE. A piece of land containing 143 square yards or thereabouts hawing a frontage of 15 feet or thereabouts to the south west side of Lugsmore-lane in ithe Township of Eccleston and forming part of the Grange Park Estate.</p>
